The [context API](https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte/blob/master/site/content/tutorial/15-context/01-context-api/text.md) in Svelte provides a way for components to communicate to each other without passing around data, functions, props, or dispatching events!

## Basic Example

```javascript
// Parent has something like:
<script>
  import { setContext } from 'svelte'
  const state = {}
  setContext('state', state)
</script>
```

```javascript
// In the descendants/child components
<script>
  import { getContext } from 'svelte'
  const state = getContext('state')
</script>
```

## The Reactivity Problem

That was easy, but say you have a situation where the context needs to be updated later in time. If we try `setTimeout(() => {setContext('state', {})}, 1000)`, this would not reflect either in the parent or the child component.

## Stores to the Rescue

`store` comes to our rescue in these cases:

```javascript
// In the parent component:
import { setContext, getContext } from 'svelte';
import { writable } from 'svelte/store';

let state = writable({color: 'hotpink'});
setContext('state', state);

setTimeout(() => { $state = {color: 'red'} }, 2000);
// ^ Setting the store value aft

After [Random images from wikipedia](http://h3manth.com/content/random-images-wikipedia) I made another simple API to get the summary for a search term using PHP.

It's a JSONP API that queries the DNS of wikipedia to fetch the TXT records, which also includes a short URL to the complete corresponding Wikipedia entry. As cross-domain requests are possible with this API, one can easily integrate it to search boxes or widgets.

**Monkey code :**

<?php  

// Set headers for JSON  
[header](http://www.php.net/header)('Content-type: application/json');  

// This the DNS to query   
$DNS=$_GET['q'].".wp.dg.cx";  

// Get the TXT records for the Name server  
$result = dns_get_record($DNS,DNS_TXT);  

// Return the JSONP  
print $_GET['callback'].'('.[json_encode](http://www.php.net/json_encode)([array](http://www.php.net/array)("res"=>$result[0]['txt'])).')';  

?>  

A simple _$.getJSON()_ can be used to get the _data.res _indeed the famous "callback=?" trick is <3'd by one and all.__

